            text-decoration: none;
        }}

        .toc a:hover {{
            text-decoration: underline;
        }}

        .number-highlight {{
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700;
        }}

        .footer {{
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px;
            color: #718096;
            font-size: 0.9em;
        }}
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="report-container">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Global Fuel Price Trends & Policy Impact Analysis</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of retail fuel prices across 84 countries, examining the interplay between Brent Crude benchmarks, taxation, subsidies, and regional economic conditions over a six-year period (2020–2026).</div>
            <div class="meta">Analysis Period: January 2020 – April 2026 | 84 Countries | 27,468 Weekly Observations</div>
        </div>

        <div class="toc">
            <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
            <ol>
                <li><a href="#overview">Global Fuel Price Overview</a></li>
                <li><a href="#temporal">Temporal Price Trends & Volatility Analysis</a></li>
                <li><a href="#regional">Regional Price Disparities</a></li>
                <li><a href="#subsidy">Impact of Subsidies and Taxation on Retail Prices</a></li>
                <li><a href="#income">Fuel Affordability by Income Level</a></li>
                <li><a href="#findings">Key Findings & Policy Implications</a></li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <section id="overview">
            <h2>1. Global Fuel Price Overview</h2>

            <p>This analysis draws upon a comprehensive dataset of weekly retail fuel prices across <strong>84 countries</strong>, spanning from January 2020 to April 2026. The dataset encompasses <strong>27,468 observations</strong>, tracking petrol, diesel, and LPG prices alongside the global Brent Crude benchmark and fiscal policy indicators.</p>

            <div class="kpi-grid">
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-value">${stats['avg_petrol']}</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Petrol Price (USD/Liter)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-value">${stats['avg_diesel']}</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Diesel Price (USD/Liter)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-value">${stats['avg_lpg']}</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. LPG Price (USD/Liter)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card highlight">
                    <div class="kpi-value">${stats['brent_avg']}</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Brent Crude (USD/Barrel)</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Price Ranges Across the Dataset</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Fuel Type</th><th>Minimum</th><th>Maximum</th><th>Range</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Petrol</td><td>${stats['petrol_range'][0]}</td><td>${stats['petrol_range'][1]}</td><td>${round(stats['petrol_range'][1] - stats['petrol_range'][0], 3)}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Diesel</td><td>${stats['diesel_range'][0]}</td><td>${stats['diesel_range'][1]}</td><td>${round(stats['diesel_range'][1] - stats['diesel_range'][0], 3)}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Brent Crude</td><td>${stats['brent_range'][0]}</td><td>${stats['brent_range'][1]}</td><td>${stats['brent_range'][1] - stats['brent_range'][0]}</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <strong>Data Note:</strong> The wide price ranges reflect significant policy-driven variation. Countries with high fuel subsidies (e.g., some Middle Eastern and African nations) show prices as low as <strong>$0.01 USD/liter</strong>, while European countries without subsidies regularly exceed <strong>$5.50 USD/liter</strong>.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="temporal">
            <h2>2. Temporal Price Trends & Volatility Analysis</h2>

            <p>The 2020–2026 period encompassed two major global energy disruptions: the <strong>COVID-19 demand collapse</strong> (2020) and the <strong>energy price crisis</strong> driven by geopolitical tensions (2022). This section examines how Brent Crude movements translated into retail fuel costs over time.</p>

            <h3>Brent Crude vs. Retail Petrol: Temporal Alignment</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['temporal_trends']}" alt="Temporal Price Trends">
                <div class="chart-caption">Figure 1: Weekly Brent Crude vs. Retail Petrol Prices (2020-2026). Notable events: COVID-19 demand collapse (Q2 2020), Energy crisis (Q1-Q2 2022), Price peak (Q2 2022).</div>
            </div>

            <h3>Annual Price Summary</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Year</th><th>Brent Crude (USD/bbl)</th><th>Petrol (USD/L)</th><th>Diesel (USD/L)</th><th>LPG (USD/L)</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>2020</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2020']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2020']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2020']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2020']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2021</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2021']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2021']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2021']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2021']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2022</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2022']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2022']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2022']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2022']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2023</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2023']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2023']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2023']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2023']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2024</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2024']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2024']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2024']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2024']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2025</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2025']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2025']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2025']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2025']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2026*</td><td>${stats['yearly']['brent_crude_usd']['2026']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['petrol_usd_liter']['2026']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['diesel_usd_liter']['2026']}</td><td>${stats['yearly']['lpg_usd_liter']['2026']}</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p><em>*2026 data through April 2026</em></p>

            <h3>Brent-to-Retail Correlation Analysis</h3>
            <p>The correlation between Brent Crude and retail petrol prices is notably <strong>weak overall</strong> (average r = {stats['avg_corr_petrol']}), indicating that local factors—subsidies, taxes, exchange rates—heavily modulate the transmission of global crude prices to consumers.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['correlation']}" alt="Correlation Analysis">
                <div class="chart-caption">Figure 2: Brent-to-Retail Petrol Correlation by Year. Note the elevated correlation in 2020 (COVID shock) versus the decoupling in later years.</div>
            </div>

            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Year</th><th>Brent-Petrol Correlation</th><th>Brent-Diesel Correlation</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>2020</td><td class="number-highlight">{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2020']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2020']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2021</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2021']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2021']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2022</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2022']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2022']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2023</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2023']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2023']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2024</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2024']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2024']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2025</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2025']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2025']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2026</td><td>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2026']}</td><td>{stats['brent_diesel_corr_by_year']['2026']}</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <div class="key-finding">
                <strong>Key Observation:</strong> The correlation peaked in 2020 at <strong>{stats['brent_petrol_corr_by_year']['2020']}</strong> during the COVID-19 demand shock, when markets moved in near-unison. Post-2021, correlations declined substantially as divergent policy responses (subsidy rollbacks, tax adjustments) created more heterogeneous retail pricing environments.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="regional">
            <h2>3. Regional Price Disparities</h2>

            <p>Fuel prices vary dramatically across geographic regions, with Europe and Oceania paying roughly <strong>3x more</strong> than the Middle East on average. This section quantifies those disparities and tracks their evolution.</p>

            <h3>Regional Average Petrol Prices</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['regional_comparison']}" alt="Regional Comparison">
                <div class="chart-caption">Figure 3: (Left) Average petrol prices by region; (Right) Evolution of regional prices over time, showing persistent structural differences.</div>
            </div>

            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Region</th><th>Avg. Price (USD/L)</th><th>Std. Deviation</th><th>Min</th><th>Max</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Europe</strong></td><td class="number-highlight">${stats['regional_avg']['mean']['Europe']}</td><td>{stats['regional_avg']['std']['Europe']}</td><td>${stats['regional_avg']['min']['Europe']}</td><td>${stats['regional_avg']['max']['Europe']}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Oceania</strong></td><td class="number-highlight">${stats['regional_avg']['mean']['Oceania']}</td><td>{stats['regional_avg']['std']['Oceania']}</td><td>${stats['regional_avg']['min']['Oceania']}</td><td>${stats['regional_avg']['max']['Oceania']}</td></tr>
