        <section id="subsidy">
            <h2>4. Impact of Subsidies and Taxation on Retail Prices</h2>

            <p>Government intervention through subsidies and taxation represents the most significant policy lever affecting retail fuel prices. This section quantifies how subsidy regimes buffer—or fail to buffer—consumers from crude oil volatility.</p>

            <h3>Subsidy Level Price Dampening Effect</h3>
            <div class="kpi-grid">
