            <div class="key-finding">
                <strong>Critical Finding:</strong> High-subsidy countries demonstrate significantly lower price volatility (σ = {stats['subsidy_volatility']['High']}) compared to low-subsidy countries (σ = {stats['subsidy_volatility']['Low']}). This confirms that robust subsidy frameworks effectively dampen crude oil pass-through to consumers. However, the fiscal cost of maintaining such subsidies is substantial and often unsustainable during prolonged high-crude-price periods.
            </div>

            <h3>Taxation Patterns by Region</h3>
